In JavaScript, a callback function is a function that you pass into another function, so that the other function can call it later.

For example : 

function greet(name, action) {
 console.log(name);
    action();
}

function sayHello() {
    console.log("Hello!");
}

greet("John", sayHello);


Here sayHello is a callback because it's a function passed as an argument and  called inside greet.
